{:edb/db-before-t 1323 :edb/db-after-t 1324 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534636 50 #inst "2026-10-08T03:02:22.559Z" 13194139534636 true] [17592186096350 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x$." 13194139534636 false] [17592186096350 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.$" 13194139534636 true] [17592186096350 1145 "At first, it may not look like we have two factors. Actually, we do, but one of them is implicit. The trick is to write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x = \\int \\ln{x} \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nUsing this trick, we can now use integration by parts. We let\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u = \\ln x & ⟹u^{′} = \\frac{1}{x} \\\\ v^{′} = 1 & ⟹v = x\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, using the by-parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\ln xdx &= x\\ln x - \\intx \\cdot \\frac{1}{x}dx \\\\\n&= x\\ln x - \\int1dx \\\\\n&= x\\ln x - x + C \\\\\n&= x(\\ln x - 1) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534636 false] [17592186096350 1145 "At first, it may not look like we have two factors. Actually, we do, but one of them is implicit. The trick is to write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x = \\int \\ln{x} \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing this trick, we can now use integration by parts. We let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the by-parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x+C \\\\  & =x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534636 true] [17592186096398 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{e} 4x\\ln\\left(x^3\\right) \\textrm{d}x$." 13194139534636 false] [17592186096398 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{e} 4x\\ln\\left(x^3\\right) \\textrm{d}x.$" 13194139534636 true] [17592186096398 1145 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and $v'$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u = \\ln (x^{3}) & ⟹u^{′} = \\frac{1}{x^{3}} \\cdot 3x^{2} = \\frac{3}{x} \\\\ v^{′} = 4x & ⟹v = \\int4xdx = 2x^{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{1}^{e}4x\\ln (x^{3})dx &= \\int_{1}^{e}uv^{′}dx \\\\\n&= \\left.uv\\right|_{1}^{e} - \\int_{1}^{e}vu^{′}dx \\\\\n&= \\ln (x^{3}) \\cdot \\left.(2x^{2})\\right|_{1}^{e} - \\int_{1}^{e}(2x^{2}) \\cdot \\frac{3}{x}dx \\\\\n&= [2(e)^{2}\\ln (e^{3}) - 2(1)^{2}\\ln (1^{3})] - 6\\int_{1}^{e}xdx \\\\\n&= 6e^{2} - \\left.6(\\frac{1}{2}x^{2})\\right|_{1}^{e} \\\\\n&= 6e^{2} - \\left.3x^{2}\\right|_{1}^{e} \\\\\n&= 6e^{2} - 3(e^{2} - 1^{2}) \\\\\n&= 3e^{2} + 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534636 false] [17592186096398 1145 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and $v',$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}=\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=4x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x=2{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot (2{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}(2{x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{3}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[2{(e)}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})-2{(1)}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{3})]-6{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-6(\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-3{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-3({e}^{2}-{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534636 true] [17592186096399 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log_4{x}}{x^3} \\,\\textrm{d}x$." 13194139534636 false] [17592186096399 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log_4{x}}{x^3} \\,\\textrm{d}x.$" 13194139534636 true] [17592186096399 1145 "We define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{4}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{4}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{4}⁡x(-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})-\\int (-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\,{log}_{4}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}(-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula $\\log_4{x}=\\dfrac{\\ln{x}}{\\ln{4}}.$" 13194139534636 true] [17592186096399 1145 "We define\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u = \\log_{4} x & ⟹u^{′} = \\frac{1}{x\\ln 4} \\\\ v^{′} = \\frac{1}{x^{3}} & ⟹v = \\int\\frac{1}{x^{3}}dx =-\\frac{1}{2x^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{\\log_{4} x}{x^{3}}dx &= \\intuv^{′}dx \\\\\n&= uv - \\intvu^{′}dx \\\\\n&= \\log_{4} x(-\\frac{1}{2x^{2}}) - \\int(-\\frac{1}{2x^{2}})\\frac{1}{x\\ln 4}dx \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{2x^{2}}\\log_{4} x + \\frac{1}{2\\ln 4}\\int\\frac{1}{x^{3}}dx \\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\ln x}{2x^{2}\\ln 4} + \\frac{1}{2\\ln 4}(-\\frac{1}{2x^{2}}) + C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\ln x}{2x^{2}\\ln 4} - \\frac{1}{4x^{2}\\ln 4} + C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2\\ln x + 1}{4x^{2}\\ln 4} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula\n\n$$\n\\log_4{x}=\\dfrac{\\ln{x}}{\\ln{4}}\n$$" 13194139534636 false] [17592186096753 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300104 13194139534636 true] [17592186096753 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300115 13194139534636 true] [17592186096753 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300119 13194139534636 true] [17592186096753 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300126 13194139534636 true] [17592186096753 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300133 13194139534636 true] [17592186096754 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300055 13194139534636 true] [17592186096754 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300062 13194139534636 true] [17592186096754 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300069 13194139534636 true] [17592186096754 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300076 13194139534636 true] [17592186096755 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300083 13194139534636 true] [17592186096755 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300090 13194139534636 true] [17592186096755 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300097 13194139534636 true] [17592186096755 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300111 13194139534636 true] [17592186096755 1020 #edb/ref 17592186300139 13194139534636 true] [17592186096977 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534636 true] [17592186096977 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{\\log_{3} x}{x^{3}}dx$." 13194139534636 false] [17592186096977 1100 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{log}_{3}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534636 true] [17592186096977 1145 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{3}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{3}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})-\\int (-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{3}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300055 1017 #edb/ref 17592186300056 13194139534636 true] [17592186300055 1089 "q-114553" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300055 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534636 true] [17592186300055 1100 "Calculate $\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300055 1113 #uuid "5e6583e6-92e6-5c07-b4f7-1730072676de" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300055 1145 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int x\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡(x)(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300057 13194139534636 true] [17592186300056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300058 13194139534636 true] [17592186300056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300059 13194139534636 true] [17592186300056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300060 13194139534636 true] [17592186300056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300061 13194139534636 true] [17592186300056 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534636 true] [17592186300056 1041 "selection" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300056 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300061 13194139534636 true] [17592186300056 1110 #uuid "12cfabff-92bf-56e2-9172-fe6f118c2de8" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300057 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300057 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534636 true] [17592186300057 1111 #uuid "4c8a9b38-30a3-52b1-9fff-2a4d191e1c43" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300058 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300058 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534636 true] [17592186300058 1111 #uuid "7a0aee70-f173-5908-827f-5f89cb4c0afb" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300059 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300059 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534636 true] [17592186300059 1111 #uuid "8c8e01d5-889e-5b4a-9acb-3c0c035897a1" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300060 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300060 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534636 true] [17592186300060 1111 #uuid "736ab1b5-d37e-536f-886c-19bb16961a18" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300061 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300061 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534636 true] [17592186300061 1111 #uuid "d3877c7f-5c76-5950-9f56-cf76e73251f7" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300062 1017 #edb/ref 17592186300063 13194139534636 true] [17592186300062 1089 "q-114555" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300062 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534636 true] [17592186300062 1100 "Calculate $\\int 8{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300062 1113 #uuid "7fe9b973-85cd-5569-aae4-2db535d24d76" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300062 1145 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=8{x}^{3}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 8{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x=2{x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 8{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\cdot (2{x}^{4})-\\int \\frac{2{x}^{4}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-2\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}+C \\\\  & ={x}^{4}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{2})+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." 13194139534636 true] [17592186300063 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300064 13194139534636 true] [17592186300063 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300065 13194139534636 true] [17592186300063 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300066 13194139534636 true] [17592186300063 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300067 13194139534636 true] [17592186300063 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300068 13194139534636 true] [17592186300063 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534636 true] [17592186300063 1041 "selection" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300063 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300065 13194139534636 true] [17592186300063 1110 #uuid "a75af52e-b616-5efd-9d80-047070c42974" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300064 1034 "{x}^{2}(\\operator