9534636 true] [17592186300083 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534636 true] [17592186300083 1100 "$\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300083 1113 #uuid "df4a8ff9-b6f1-509e-8da7-ab67f79ced45" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300083 1145 "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}=\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{3}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." 13194139534636 true] [17592186300084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300085 13194139534636 true] [17592186300084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300086 13194139534636 true] [17592186300084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300087 13194139534636 true] [17592186300084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300088 13194139534636 true] [17592186300084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300089 13194139534636 true] [17592186300084 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534636 true] [17592186300084 1041 "selection" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300084 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300089 13194139534636 true] [17592186300084 1110 #uuid "507e7950-22fa-5522-8d6e-e608954b5950" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300085 1034 "3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+x+C" 13194139534636 true] [17592186300085 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534636 true] [17592186300085 1111 #uuid "4c0aef57-abe2-5e9b-8ffd-b4